ion roguelite in the survivors-like style. The player picks one of sixteen heroes, whose weapon attacks on its own, and steers through growing monster hordes, collecting experience to level up. Movement is the player's main input: heroes run, jump and slide, and each has a movement ability of their own. Level-ups come as booster packs of upgrade cards; two upgrades can be fused into a new attack, and items stack on top. The first chapter's campaign runs from the Keep through crypts beneath an estate to the Cinder Reach and back, with a choice of routes and bosses including the Rat King. It supports single player and online co-op for two to four players (in beta).", "themes": [{"id": 1, "name": "Action"}, {"id": 17, "name": "Fantasy"}, {"id": 19, "name": "Horror"}, {"id": 27, "name": "Comedy"}], "url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/there-goes-the-kingdom", "videos": [{"id": 203707, "name": "Trailer", "video_id": "drrfqmVcy34", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=drrfqmVcy34", "title": "There Goes the Kingdom \u2013 Gameplay Trailer", "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/drrfqmVcy34/maxresdefault.jpg"}]}